{ev[\"Tokens\"][3][\"CreatedBy\"],
  FirstPosition[#[\"Consumed\"] & /@ ev[\"Events\"], 3][[1]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"dbef3868-0dfc-9f4c-8f31-582c9c3b5096"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "3"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"f252ad17-6d4d-9943-947d-8c610459ab35"],

Cell["\<\
Event 1 made it and event 3 used it, so there is an arrow from 1 to 3 in the \
causal graph \[LongDash] and there it is:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a82ab1cf-36c7-f44a-80c2-8027a28c37f7"],

Cell["\<\
MemberQ[EdgeList @ ev[\"CausalGraph\", \"Draw\" -> False], DirectedEdge[1, 3]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fd6532a3-2266-f44f-9970-9a8b1edc4ef3"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"df0f5cb6-0afe-8d4f-8d27-48fe3e44cade"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Because a token knows both ends of its own story, nothing has to be \
searched for. Two events on different branches can never be joined, since a \
token created on one branch is only ever in the states that descend from it. \
The whole causal graph is one pass over the tokens."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"aeae7902-6b1f-0d41-b4b5-ff85e640abac"],

Cell["\<\
The two events of the first step, by contrast, share nothing \[LongDash] they \
are two things that could have happened, not two that did:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fb5602ca-1bf5-5340-a651-ee54984a8f72"],

Cell["{#[\"Consumed\"], #[\"Created\"]} & /@ Take[ev[\"Events\"], 2]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5249383d-91aa-244e-b070-8873d1a815f0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"5", ",", "6"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUU\
ID->"997cca08-36b3-564a-a247-84b80764e237"],

Cell["5. A labelled system", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c1460067-c959-ff42-acbb-65ae36db1df9"],

Cell["\<\
Nothing is particular to unlabelled hypergraphs. Composition of labelled \
arrows, which is the rule the reference notebooks are written around:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b717464-4354-5d45-bd98-2c298f4efb27"],

Cell["\<\
comp = HypergraphRule[
  {Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", x], Edge[{2, 3}, \"Directed\", y]},
  {Edge[{1, 3}, \"Directed\", Row[{\"(\", x, y, \")\"}]]}];
chain = Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", a], Edge[{2, 3}, \"Directed\", \
b],
                    Edge[{3, 4}, \"Directed\", c]}];
lsys = RewritingSystem[comp, chain]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0e05f81d-072f-fe47-b557-3521102a9777"],

